{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1773846755,"nonce":"ZLYE8W05ABBvk4sDp+sbbxtu3kw=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM7zYp3O","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/6#issuecomment-4083326414"},"message":"## Network Diagram Plan\n\nThe goal is a side-by-side diagram — operator on the left, boat on the right — with the two data paths (WiFi and VPN) running between them horizontally.\n\n### Layout\n\n```\n[ Operator side ]  ←—— WiFi backhaul (172.16.12.0/24) ——→  [ Boat side ]\n                   ←—————— VPN (via internet/cloud) ————→\n```\n\n**Operator side** — operator LAN `192.168.13.0/24`:\n- Operator laptop\n- Development laptop\n- Operator router\n\n**Boat side** — onboard LAN `192.168.12.0/24`:\n- Robot computer (Linux)\n- Windows PC\n- Camera\n- POS MV\n- Boat router\n- DeltaT sonar on its own subnet (`192.168.0.0/24`)\n- ArduPilot FCU shown as a USB connection on the robot computer (no IP)\n\n**WiFi backhaul** — `172.16.12.0/24` between the two routers, shown as background infrastructure rather than a focal element.\n\n**VPN path** — shown as a line arcing through a cloud/internet symbol. The NETMAP subnets are annotated here since they define how users address devices over this path:\n- To reach a boat device via VPN → use `192.168.14.x` (maps to `192.168.12.x`)\n- To reach an operator device via VPN → use `192.168.15.x` (maps to `192.168.13.x`)\n\n### Format Options\n\n**Graphviz DOT** — `rankdir=LR`, `cluster_` subgraphs per subnet, output as SVG embedded in the README. Plain-text source lives in the repo and can be regenerated. Good layout control for the side-by-side structure.\n\n**Draw.io** — most visual flexibility: colored subnet boxes, native cloud shape for the VPN/internet path, transparent styling for the WiFi backhaul zone. The `.drawio` file lives in the repo; a PNG/SVG export is embedded in the README.\n\nEither works; Draw.io gives more polish for the cloud shape and the transparent backhaul zone, Graphviz is more scriptable.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `claude-sonnet-4-6`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1773846854,"nonce":"p/PGVpvVqrePLRdwZj1uXiww5Qs=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM7zYtDR","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/6#issuecomment-4083339473"},"message":"Also a windows machine on the operator side for survey monitoring.\nAdd the subnet used over the vpn\nprobably use dot","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1773847048,"nonce":"YkWKUOgYokCd7GFgOblPcfrJWn0=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM7zYzuq","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/6#issuecomment-4083366826"},"message":"## Review\n\n### Scope Assessment\n\n**Well-scoped?** Yes — a single diagram file plus embedding it in the docs is a clear, bounded deliverable. The comments on this issue have done good work narrowing the scope (role names over hostnames, subnets not specific IPs, Graphviz DOT format, layout decided). One gap: the refinements from the comments aren't captured in the issue body. Worth updating the body before implementation begins so the spec is self-contained.\n\n**Right repo?** Yes — platform-specific documentation belongs in `unh_echoboats_project11`.\n\n**Dependencies:** The source material (`docs/izzyboat_network.md`) already exists on the `feature/issue-2` branch. This issue's work can branch from `jazzy` independently, but should note that the network doc it references was produced by issue #2.\n\n**Output placement not specified:** The issue doesn't say where the diagram lives or how it gets referenced. Suggest: `.dot` source + generated SVG both committed to `docs/`, referenced from either the network doc or a README.\n\n### Principle Alignment\n\n| Principle | Status | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Only what's needed | OK | Scope has been deliberately trimmed — role names, subnets only, one diagram |\n| A change includes its consequences | Watch | The diagram needs to be linked/embedded somewhere; the issue doesn't specify where. Should be resolved before or during implementation |\n| Capture decisions, not just implementations | OK | No architectural decision being made; documentation artifact only |\n| Human control and transparency | OK | Diagram improves transparency of the network setup |\n| Improve incrementally | OK | Single deliverable, small PR |\n| Workspace vs. project separation | OK | Correctly scoped to the project repo |\n\n### ADR Applicability\n\n| ADR | Triggered | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0002 — Worktree isolation | Yes | Implementation needs its own worktree for issue #6; do not reuse the issue-2 worktree |\n| 0008 — ROS 2 conventions | No | Documentation only, no packages |\n| All others | No | Not applicable |\n\n### Consequences\n\n- The `.dot` source file and generated SVG should both be committed so the diagram is both maintainable and renderable\n- The diagram should be linked from `docs/izzyboat_network.md` and/or a package README so it's discoverable\n- If the network doc (`feature/issue-2`) is updated in future, the diagram may need to follow\n\n### Recommendations\n\n- Update the issue body to capture the layout decisions from the comments (Graphviz DOT, side-by-side layout, NETMAP annotation, Windows machine on operator side) so the spec is self-contained\n- Decide and state where the output is referenced (network doc, README, or both) before starting\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `claude-sonnet-4-6`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1773847214,"nonce":"UVxL3AEDxacH8SSE/Q/XjwPtgSg=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM7zY5Tq","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/6#issuecomment-4083389674"},"message":"Let's reference the diagram in both the network doc and readme","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1775517382,"nonce":"KPwl2YMH5iKG3jHOo/yI9ulzVCE=","metadata":{